    <div class="body-copy reveal">
      <p>I'm a product and experience designer based in Houston, Texas. Over the past several years I've focused on UX and product design, most recently as an Experience Lead at Merkle, helping teams turn complex business challenges into simple, human-centered solutions — shaping strategy, running workshops, and coaching designers along the way.</p>
      <p>My path started in industrial design (B.S., University of Houston, with a minor in Architecture), designing housewares, exhibits and prototypes before moving into digital. I still love designing physical products alongside digital ones. That mix of screen and object shapes how I think — how something works matters just as much as how it feels in your hands.</p>
      <p>When I'm not designing, you'll usually find me under a car, fixing anything from a flat tire to a blown piston. It's the same instinct that drives my design work: take something apart, understand what makes it tick, and make it run better.</p>
      <div class="quote-row">
        <p class="quote">"Design is an ever-changing environment; adapting to those changes keeps me excited. Every project is different — and that variety is what I love about the work."</p>
      </div>
